## 2. Wire env (per environment, secrets via stdin)

```bash
vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL production           # https://{{project}}.vercel.app FIRST
vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL production
vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLIC_KEY production
printf '%s' "$SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY" | vercel env add SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY production
# repeat for preview; add development vars in a SEPARATE command (cannot combine dev with prod/preview)
```

Note: prod/preview vars are stored `sensitive` and cannot be read back via `vercel env ls`. Verify at runtime (smoke check, section 5), not by listing.

## 3. Push Supabase to cloud

```bash
export SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_...
npx -y supabase@latest link --project-ref {{supabase_project_ref}}
supabase db pull          # drift check; review the generated remote-schema migration
supabase db push          # apply migrations
supabase migration list   # confirm Local == Remote
supabase functions deploy # deploy Edge Functions
supabase secrets set {{external_secret}}=...   # external secrets only (URL/keys auto-injected)
```

## 4. Trigger the deploy

```bash
vercel --prod --yes
```

Wait for Ready. Then run the smoke check (Ready is not working).

## 5. Smoke check (go/no-go, 5 to 15 min)

Run `templates/smoke-check.sh` or these four checks:

1. Homepage 200: `curl -sD - https://{{domain}}/ | grep -iE 'HTTP/|location'`  (a 307 to /sign-in is OK only if /sign-in is built).
2. Auth-gated route `{{auth_route}}` redirects to sign-in, and sign-in returns 200.
3. DB-touching route `{{db_route}}` returns real data within the serverless timeout (10s Hobby / 15s Pro).
4. Auth callback URL resolves.

<!-- TODO: fill in {{auth_route}} and {{db_route}} for this app -->

## 6. Cutover order (staged, reversible)

1. Deploy on `https://{{project}}.vercel.app` (Site URL set to vercel.app).
2. Rotate Supabase keys one client at a time (both keys work simultaneously); deactivate legacy last.
3. Supabase Auth URL config: Site URL `https://{{domain}}`, Redirect URLs `https://{{domain}}/auth/callback**`, preview wildcard `https://*-{{project}}.vercel.app/auth/callback**`.
4. Swap `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` to `https://{{domain}}`, attach domain, redeploy, re-verify.

Re-run the smoke check after EACH stage.

## 7. Rollback

| Stage | Rollback |
|---|---|
| Site URL | revert `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`, redeploy |
| Key rotation | point the client back to the old key (still active) |
| Auth URLs | restore previous Site URL / Redirect URLs |
| Custom domain | revert to vercel.app Site URL, redeploy |
